{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='metadata.json';m=json.load(open(p))\nm['sourceInformation']['testing']='103 automated checks: 17 real Rapier campaign checks plus 86 browser and official AI Hub harness checks. Scripted full patrol with real steering, lasers and torpedoes; emulated standard gamepad and touch; synthesized-audio analyser; local ghost pilots; 2-player and 4-player Hub rounds including 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter, 5% packet loss and host departure; file:// launch. Native WebGPU flight/input checks and WebGL compatibility multiplayer/touch checks. Visual QA at 1440×900, 1920×1080 and mobile sizes. No physical controller, real touch hardware, TV or human listening.'\nm['testingFeedback']=['13 functional issues were found and fixed, plus two readability improvements. They covered physics initialization and cleanup, texture upload, menu focus/navigation, pointer drift, Hub countdown/debrief lifecycle, permanent starbase loss and docking state/scoring.','3 were game breaking for a supported path: physics initialization, invalid WebGPU texture upload and controller hyperspace confirmation. All were fixed.','The complete four-sector campaign using actual steering, lasers and homing torpedoes, followed by the official AI Hub conformance runs under loss, latency and host departure.','Fixed-duration browser waits were least useful: software rendering made them unreliable. The final checks wait for observed frames and game state.']\nm['engineFeedback']=['Three.js native AnimationMixer clips and toon node materials worked well for animated procedural ships, reactors and the rotating starbase.','I initially used an incorrect Rapier descriptor method and an unsupported RGB texture upload. Tests caught both. The workstation’s software WebGPU also needed an explicit ANGLE backend flag.','The flight campaign, tactical sector chart, targeting, cross-device input interface and ghost-pilot lifecycle.','Validating WebGPU headlessly: native GPU state checks and compatibility-renderer screenshots were both needed because headless WebGPU screenshots omitted the canvas.','none','Provide a stable, documented headless WebGPU capture and validation path across software adapters.']\nm['promptFeedback']=['The source, single-file deliverable, attract mode and live tuning requirements gave the game a clear, practical shape.','The intended Star Raiders edition and the preferred standalone multiplayer mode were not specified. The supplied year was retained; ghost competition was chosen.','Completing a flight campaign, strategic layer, synthesized audio, device controls and multiplayer lifecycle in one shareable document.','Specify a target mission duration and preferred multiplayer relationship, such as cooperative, competitive or ghost-based.']\nopen(p,'w').write(json.dumps(m,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nopen('../exit-interview.json','w').write(json.dumps(m,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\njson.load(open('../exit-interview.json'))\nPY\nnpm run build && node verify.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"agent_message","text":"All **103 checks passed**, including the three official Hub scenarios and opening the single HTML through `file://`. The final build includes the completed credits and exit interview. I’m running the same check command once more after the last navigation-prompt and destroyed-starbase display changes.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,hashlib\nroot=Path('..'); stem='Stellar-Raiders-Star-Raiders-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-223041'\nh=root/(stem+'.html'); d=json.loads((root/'exit-interview.json').read_text()); m=json.loads(Path('metadata.json').read_text())\nassert d==m\nassert set(d)=={'sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub'}\nassert [len(d[k]) for k in ['testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback']]==[4,6,4]\nassert len(d['sourceInformation'])==15\nassert all(isinstance(v,str) and v for v in d['sourceInformation'].values())\ns=h.read_text(); session=Path('hub-session.js').read_text(); assert s[s.index('<script>')+8:s.index('</script>')]==session\nassert 'Testing in progress' not in s\nassert h.read_bytes()==Path('game.html').read_bytes()\nprint('Release and exit interview validated; HTML bytes:',h.stat().st_size)\np=root/'.game-folder'\nif p.exists():p.unlink()\nprogress=json.loads(Path('browser-progress.json').read_text()); print('Final verification progress:',len(progress),progress[-1]['name']);print('Failures:',[x for x in progress if not x['pass']])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
